WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.900
When an app stops responding, someone has to work out
what changed.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.180
AURA helps small teams investigate and recover the
applications they run in Docker.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:20.690
Here's Linkding. We've saved its working settings and
given AURA permission to restore them automatically.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.300
For this test, we deliberately change the app's port.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.100
The container keeps running, but requests stop reaching
it.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.180
AURA notices the failed checks and starts
investigating.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:42.250
Two agents using Meta's Open 1026 model examine the
runtime and configuration.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.930
A third combines their findings into a proposed action.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.370
The app is listening on a different port from its saved
configuration.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.130
Restarting it would leave that setting unchanged.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.460
AURA checks the proposal against our permissions and
restores the saved settings.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.580
It then sends real requests to confirm that the app
responds again.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.520
In this run, recovery was confirmed in 93 seconds using
three model calls.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.200
We didn't intervene after introducing the fault.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.640
We also tested a separate memory problem.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:29.340
The generated code fix needed a correction during human
review.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.600
AURA then tested and deployed the approved version.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.480
Both large files downloaded in full with their contents
verified.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.500
The findings, changes, and verification results stay
available for review.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.160
New apps start in observation mode.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.640
You choose which recovery actions AURA can take
automatically.
